# Local development only (`npm run dev`); CRA reads it, but exposes only
# REACT_APP_* names to the bundle.
# Server-side settings live in backend/.env (see backend/.env.example), and
# Docker uses .env.docker plus .env.db, the database password only (see README
# "Docker Setup" and .env.db.example).

# The Python that runs Django for `npm run dev` / `npm start` / `npm run django`
# (scripts/run-django.js). Use the environment with backend/requirements.txt
# installed, e.g. a dedicated Conda env's python.exe. A shell variable of the
# same name wins over this file; unset falls back to `python` on the PATH.
# DJANGO_PYTHON=/path/to/envs/cinedb/python

# Uncomment for LAN access to `npm run dev` from another device.
# `::` listens on IPv6 and IPv4 alike. Don't use 0.0.0.0 (IPv4 only): where
# `localhost` resolves to ::1 first, every new browser connection to
# localhost:3000 then waits ~200-300 ms for the IPv4 fallback, and with the dev
# `proxy` (package.json) all API calls ride those connections.
# HOST=::
# DANGEROUSLY_DISABLE_HOST_CHECK=true
